// Ziy extension suite.
//
// ONE SOURCE OF TRUTH for the add-on ids shipped in the Ziy suite. The ids are
// derived from the filename, not the manifest — XPIProvider.sys.mjs's
// getExpectedID() turns "ziy-shields@ziy.app.xpi" into the add-on id
// "ziy-shields@ziy.app". That is why distribution/extensions/ must contain
// files named exactly `<id>.xpi`, and why ids in this list, in
// distribution/policies.json and in native messaging manifests have to agree.
//
// Consumed by: tools/build-shell.sh, tools/verify.sh, native/manifest writers.
// Format: one id per line, '#" comments allowed. No extension is built in the
// shell slice; the suite is filled in by tools/build-extension.sh later.

ziy-shell@ziy.app
ziy-shields@ziy.app
ziy-ntp@ziy.app
ziy-news@ziy.app
ziy-playlist@ziy.app
ziy-talk@ziy.app
ziy-sync@ziy.app
ziy-desktop@ziy.app
ziy-pwd@ziy.app
